  {
    "id": "vue-components/range#overview",
    "documentId": "vue-components/range",
    "heading": "Range",
    "breadcrumb": [
      "Range"
    ],
    "level": 1,
    "canonicalUrl": "https://quasar.dev/vue-components/range",
    "content": "The QRange component is a great way to offer the user the selection of a sub-range of values between a minimum and maximum value, with optional steps to select those values. An example use case for the Range component would be to offer a price range selection.\n\nAlso check out its “sibling”, the [QSlider](/vue-components/slider) component.\n\nAPI reference: QRange",
    "apiReferences": [
      "QRange"
    ],
    "exampleReferences": []
  },
  {
    "id": "vue-components/range#usage",
    "documentId": "vue-components/range",
    "heading": "Usage",
    "breadcrumb": [
      "Usage",
      "Usage"
    ],
    "level": 2,
    "canonicalUrl": "https://quasar.dev/vue-components/range#usage",
    "content": "Notice we are using an object for the selection, which holds values for both the lower value of the selected range - `rangeValues.min` and the higher value - `rangeValues.max`.",
    "apiReferences": [],
    "exampleReferences": []
  },
